  <dashboards>
    <dashboard _.fcp.AccessibleZoneTabOrder.true...enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Info'>
      <repository-location derived-from='http://ip-172-31-0-132:8885/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/DM-Operations-SCM-IDPSKUVisualiser/Info?rev=' id='Info' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/DM-Operations-SCM-IDPSKUVisualiser' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style />
      <size maxheight='1000' maxwidth='1200' minheight='1000' minwidth='1200' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='98400' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98666' x='667' y='800'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>The aim of this Dashbord is o help Demand Planners to have greater visibility over the forecasts generated from IDP to ascertain where the model may fail and apply corrective action. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Data owner: Tatiana Ovchinnikova</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Source: </run>
              <run fontcolor='#1a1a1a' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>rl_dmart.idp_sku_visualiser</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run auto-url='true' fontcolor='#4996b2' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://github.com/deliveryhero/datahub-airflow/blob/main/dags/dmart/curated_data_report/sql/reports/idp_sku_visualiser.sql&amp;quot;'>https://github.com/deliveryhero/datahub-airflow/blob/main/dags/dmart/curated_data_report/sql/reports/idp_sku_visualiser.sql</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Update: daily</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Scope: </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>- included countries that have IPD forecast.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>- included skus, that were available at least once during last 60 days.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='14'>Metrics and definitions</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Predicted Qty Baseline</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'> - initial forecast based on previous sales and availability</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Predicted Qty Effective</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'> - Predicted Qty Baseline + Promo Uplift </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Predicted Qty Corrected</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'> - Predicted Qty Effective with Forecast Factor</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Supplier</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'> - preffered supllier</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>WAPE (Weighted Absolute Percentage Error)</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>The metrics help us provide an overarching sense of how the model is performing. It measures the accuracy of the mean forecast. In order to better reflect what our forecast error is when aggregated to match an average purchasing cycle, we smooth the error by aggregating it over a 7 day rolling window.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Forecast Bias, %</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>The metric helps us to understand if the model is consistently under-forecasting or over-forecasting. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>= forecast qty / sold qty</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Availability.</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'> % </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>- weighted availability</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>- hourly availibility - share of hours when product was available during the whole day</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>- hourly availibility (working hours) - share of hours when product was available during working hours of the store</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Shrinkage</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Shrinkage, % qty - qty of written-off items (stock movements with reason &apos;expiry&apos;) / sold qty</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Shrinkage, % revenue - cost of written-off items (stock movements with reason &apos;expiry&apos;) / total revenue</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic'>FILTERS</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>ABC Segment: </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>- A: product contributes to top 50% of sales </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>- B: product falls into 50%-85% sales contribution </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>- C: product contributes bottom 15% of sales </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>XYZ Segment: </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>This is calculated using a variability coefficient calculated over the last 30 days of daily sales as stddev/mean </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>-X: low variability coefficient, between 0 and 0.5 </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>-Y: medium variability coefficient, between 0.5 and 1..</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>-Z: high variability coefficient, greater than 1</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Is active:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'> whether the product has current active status.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1d1c1d' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>Future promo</run>
              <run fontcolor='#1d1c1d' fontname='Segoe UI Historic' fontsize='10'>.  Set to &apos;true&apos; it will show only skus, that have a promo uplift in the forecast for any day starting from today.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
